WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.890
My name is Yuma Tsukumo!

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.260
I’m a first-year middle school student who’s
gonna become duel champion by kattobing!

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.440
What? You’re going to
give me Baby Tiragon?

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.030
That’s an Xyz Monster!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.450
Don’t take cards from Tokunosuke, Yuma.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.660
There’s always something
behind what he does!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.570
You guys are too suspicious.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.500
But you were
tricked in the end.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.840
If you lose this duel, he’ll take
your Number Card due to the ante rule.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.880
Why, Tokunosuke?

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.350
I thought you were my friend!

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:37.320
He stole Utopia!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.860
I tricked you!

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:50.570
As long as the Continuous Trap Ultra C
is on my field, I’ll win this duel!

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.610
When I win, I’ll take
Utopia as promised!

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.110
You planned to take my
Number from the start!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.540
Tokunosuke!

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:15.050
I don’t know why, but power
is surging through my body.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.510
What’s happening?

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.400
A Number took over his body.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.730
Number?

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.130
39!

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.120
That’s Utopia’s number!

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.460
Tokunosuke...

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:42.410
What’s wrong?

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.460
My body...

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:49.250
What are those threads of light?

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:56.260
If you don’t win this duel,
I will vanish from this world.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:01.070
Is he starting to vanish
because I accepted this duel?

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:03.060
What are you doing?

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.980
Hurry up and end your turn.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.030
I have to win this duel.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.900
Only a Number can
defeat a Number.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.160
I have the Numbers Leviathan
Dragon and Terror-Byte.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.950
Level 4 Gagaga and Level
2 Full Elf are on my field.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.100
It’s no good.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.960
I can’t Xyz Summon
with these two monsters!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.160
I end my turn!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.800
Looks like you’re giving up.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.080
I’ll finish you in an instant!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.310
My turn! I draw!

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.130
Utopia attacks Full Elf!

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.640
Hope Sword Slash!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.980
It’s now 2500 vs. 1900 LP.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.940
I made a comeback!

00:02:57.940 --> 00:03:01.950
I set a monster in face-down
defense position and end my turn!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.660
If I don’t summon
a Number soon, I’ll lose!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.080
My turn! I draw!

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.830
All right! I have it!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.000
I can summon a Number!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.630
I summon Level 3 Rai Rider!

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.680
Then I activate Gagaga Magician’s effect!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:35.150
Once per turn, I can change this card’s
Level to any between 1 and 8 until the End Phase.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.570
I change Gagaga Magician
to Level 3, just like Rai Rider.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.070
Here I go!

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.780
I overlay Level 3 Gagaga
Magician and Rai Rider!

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.190
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.600
Xyz Summon!

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.930
Appear, Number 17: Leviathan Dragon!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.480
Number 17?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.010
There are other Numbers?

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.780
Then I’ll take it too!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.990
I activate the Continuous
Trap Traitor Fog!

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.310
What’s this fog?

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.600
It’s Traitor Fog’s fog.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.840
Due to the Continuous Trap Traitor Fog,
when a monster is Special Summoned onto your field...

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.050
I gain control of that monster.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.220
Leviathan Dragon!

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.940
It’s here!

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.190
No way! Leviathan Dragon too?

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.870
Astral!

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.670
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:19.790
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.590
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.970
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:34.350
In truth, I was sad
until I met you

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:40.800
I lied, thinking it was
easier to be alone

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:47.450
Even though we don’t like
the same books or hobbies

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:51.330
You’re the only one
who agreed with me

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.450
Joy and sadness and anger
and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.230
There’s no harmony and scenario
without differences

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.540
Everyone is not the same

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:04.550
That’s the reason for living

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:09.800
Even if the sounds
are dissonant at times

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:15.220
That’s why I never give up!
I believe my strength will get me through

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:19.030
I travel to
the edge of the world

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:22.940
The sights I see
with you are the truth

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.780
Whether it’s rain, wind,
blizzard or the scorching sun

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.030
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:32.410
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:36.080
Freedom begins by accepting differences
Dance and create the universe

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.880
Traitorous Numbers?!

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.880
Number 6:

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.880
Traitorous Numbers?!

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.350
Just like I thought!

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:55.840
This photo is a fake!

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.930
Different photos were pasted together!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.150
This one too!

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.280
And this!

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.560
They’re all composites!

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.220
We can prove Yuma’s innocence!

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.460
But who would do this?

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.910
Oh yeah! Taichi!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.170
Taichi might know something.

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:18.660
Maybe Taichi is in on this.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.750
Taichi, it’s Kotori.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.590
What do you want?

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.750
I want to ask you something.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.360
I’m busy!

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.170
Taichi!

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.600
Next time!

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.440
He hung up.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.600
I heard chimes in the background!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.140
Astral! Hey, Astral!

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.560
Astral...

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.820
He’s talking to himself again.

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.790
Yuma, admit that you lost!

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.620
Blame yourself for getting tricked!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:59.040
Why do do you need to win so badly
that you have to trick people?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.370
Isn’t it obvious?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.890
There’s no point to dueling
if I don’t win!

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.240
That’s how the world works!

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.500
I know that best!

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:12.630
It was when I first
started dueling.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.030
Toku, you’ve started dueling?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.600
Want us to teach you?

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.310
Really?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.560
But using the ante rule.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.990
Ante rule?

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:24.280
It’s a betting duel.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.300
The winner gets to take
a card from the loser.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.820
Take?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.730
It’ll force you to duel seriously,
so you’ll improve faster.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:35.780
We‘re only thinking
of what’s best for you, Toku.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.290
But that was a lie.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:49.310
They took cards from me every day.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:54.150
That idiot doesn’t know
that he’s being ripped off.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.830
Thanks to him,
we have a lot of good cards.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:02.140
That’s when I learned that there’s always
something going on behind-the-scenes.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:06.650
The nicer people are,
the more shenanigans are taking place.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:17.870
That’s why I decided to master
the behind-the-scenes world!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.660
Tokunosuke...

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.210
Taichi!

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.080
He’s not here.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.160
But he’s somewhere at school.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.550
Taichi!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.640
Taichi!

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:39.890
I vowed to use the behind-the-scenes
world to get my revenge.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:45.600
Day and night, I practiced card switching
techniques until I mastered them.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.630
And I took back
my stolen cards.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.740
I didn’t care
if people hated me.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.740
The world is full of shenanigans.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.240
When I win, they wag their tails
and approach me.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.910
That’s human nature.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.930
That’s life!

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.290
It’s all lies
if you don’t win!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.880
Even in a duel,
winning is everything!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.160
That’s not what
a duel is about!

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.140
Winning isn’t everything!

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:18.400
A duel is a clash
between hearts!

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:23.010
They keep making fun of you for being a bad player
because you say things like that.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.560
I can’t find him.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.930
Same here.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.700
Where haven’t we searched yet?

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:33.270
The old gymnasium!

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:35.250
He must be there!

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.530
Taichi...

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:39.280
I’ll make him tell
us who’s the culprit!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:44.450
Taichi!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.730
I was so close!

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.000
How could you do this?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.260
I’m sorry!

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:18.090
I didn’t know you
were lining up dominoes!

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:21.490
But why are you lining
up dominoes here?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:26.650
If I line them all up, Tokunosuke said
that he would give me an Xyz Monster.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:28.450
So I’ve been lining them up
since this morning.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.750
Tokunosuke?

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.270
Just like I thought.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.710
Tokunosuke is the culprit.

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:38.300
That means...

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:40.470
Yuma!

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:45.410
The only Number I have left
is Terror-Byte.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.640
In that case,
I’ll use this spell card.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:55.540
When there’s only one monster on my field,
Release Lease tributes that monster.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:12:01.620
By doing so, I can add one Level
3 monster in my deck to my hand.

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.660
Okay, I’ll tribute Baby Tiragon!

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.240
Protect Baby Tiragon.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:10.740
Protect it.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:12.580
Are you okay?

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.750
Baby Tiragon...

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.800
But Baby Tiragon
can’t defeat a Number!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.340
Baby Tiragon...

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:31.890
I switch Baby Tiragon
to defense position!

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:39.400
I set one card
and end my turn!

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.400
You think that strengthened your defense?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.490
That was pointless.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.460
My turn! I draw!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.930
Where did Yuma go?

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:56.010
Let’s try the shopping mall!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.170
I activate Leviathan Dragon’s effect!

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:08.600
Once per turn, it gains 500 ATK
by using an Overlay Unit!

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.600
Next up is a Flip Summon!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.460
Flip Summon?

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:20.280
I switch a face-down defense position monster
into face-up attack position.

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:24.860
In other words, I can use its flip
effect even though it wasn’t attacked!

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:28.620
Appear, Flipangutan!

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:37.030
Flipangutan’s flip effect activates!

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:40.550
It switches a monster
from defense position to attack position!

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:49.300
Baby Tiragon is back
in attack position!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:54.130
Leviathan Dragon attacks Baby Tiragon!

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.980
Vice Stream!

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.560
I activate the trap Half Unbreak!

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:10.290
With Half Unbreak, my monster isn’t destroyed
in battle this turn, and I only take half the damage!

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.400
So you had that trap.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.870
But Utopia has 2500 ATK.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:25.270
Even if I only deal half
damage, that’s enough!

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:29.010
Go, Utopia!

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.470
Hope Sword Slash!

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:45.290
I activate the spell card
Book of Flip from my hand!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:51.990
This card switches a Flip Monster
into face-down defense position!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.200
Now I can use its
flip effect again.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.590
That means even if I switch Baby Tiragon
to defense position on my next turn...

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:04.670
...Flipangutan’s flip effect will change it back
to attack position, and I’ll take battle damage!

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.580
Correct.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.270
That’s perceptive of you, Yuma.

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:12.760
You only have 300 LP left.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.340
It’s over on my next turn.

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:16.430
I end my turn.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:17.800
Damn!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.100
Yuma!

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.900
Kotori! Tetsuo!

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.730
Yuma, what’s going on?

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.240
You’ve arrived too late.

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.690
It’s over.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.740
2500 vs. 300?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:36.580
And why are Utopia and Leviathan
Dragon on Tokunosuke’s field?

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:40.000
Yuma, it’s your turn.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.850
I only have 300
LP left!

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:44.970
I have to strengthen my defense!

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.090
My turn! I draw!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.620
Stinging Swordsman?

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:52.390
It’s no good. I can’t
protect myself with this.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:57.270
Looks like you didn’t get
the card you wanted.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:00.800
I’m going to lose without kattobing?

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.090
Yuma...

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:05.700
It’s pointless to think!

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:13.260
You only have Rank 1 Baby Tiragon,
the worst Xyz Monster!

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.160
There’s nothing you can do.

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.890
Is there nothing I can do?

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.680
Protect it.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:23.420
Why does he want to
protect Baby Tiragon?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.100
I see!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.380
I get it!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:30.090
Here I go!

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.800
Baby Tiragon!

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:36.760
I summon Stinging Swordsman!

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.290
300 ATK?

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:44.450
What can you do
with that card?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:48.230
I can do something
when it’s paired with Baby Tiragon!

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:50.260
With that garbage card?

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.110
I’m kattobing!

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.910
Baby Tiragon’s effect activates!

00:16:55.910 --> 00:17:02.330
By using one Overlay Unit,
one Level 1 monster can attack you directly!

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.170
Go, Stinging Swordsman!

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.540
Attack Tokunosuke directly!

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.790
But that’s only 300
points of damage.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.930
It doesn’t hurt at all.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:17.800
That was pointless!

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.730
Now’s my chance!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:30.940
Stinging Swordsman’s effect activates!

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:35.160
Hurricane!

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.980
What?

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:46.450
When Stinging Swordsman attacks you directly,
all face-up spell and trap cards on your field return to your hand!

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:47.580
All?

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:48.380
That’s right!

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:54.470
If the cards that stole Utopia
and Leviathan Dragon are removed from your field...

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:57.930
...they return to me!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.110
My Numbers!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:19.120
All right!

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:21.330
I retrieved my Numbers!

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.560
Are you okay?

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:37.980
I’m going to win.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:42.880
Leviathan Dragon, attack
the face-down defense position monster!

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.970
It’s my duel!

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.440
Go, Leviathan Dragon!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:53.150
Attack the face-down defense position monster!

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.760
Vice Stream!

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.600
He did it!

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.160
Nice! Now he doesn’t have
any defending monsters!

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.890
Utopia, attack him directly!

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.510
Go!

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.590
Hope Sword Slash!

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.190
All right! It’s over!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.190
He won!

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.150
You did it, Yuma!

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:45.620
Thank you for shopping here today.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:46.930
Well done.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.950
You protected the Numbers.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.840
I didn’t do it for you!

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:53.330
Yuma!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.940
That was an incredible turnaround!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:58.800
It’s thanks to Baby Tiragon!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.660
I lost.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.870
Why?

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.760
Tokunosuke...

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.840
I’m giving this back.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:09.730
That’s...

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.940
It’s your card.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.070
In exchange, don’t cheat anymore.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:17.370
You’re making Baby Tiragon sad.

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.070
But you’re tough!

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:22.780
I’m tough?

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.760
Yeah!

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:29.360
I’ve never met anyone who’s
a master of Flip Monsters like you!

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:30.750
Yuma...

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.610
You can’t fool me.

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:36.690
What’s your purpose
for cheering me up?

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:37.510
Purpose?

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:39.050
I have no purpose.

00:20:39.050 --> 00:20:42.190
I said you’re tough
because that’s what I believe!

00:20:42.190 --> 00:20:44.690
I don’t believe you.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:49.100
Are you serious?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.480
Of course!

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.560
Yuma!

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:03.510
It’s the first time
anyone said that I’m tough!

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:09.050
They always call me a cheater
or that I’m dirty!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:13.110
Keep that card!

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:14.960
It’s a symbol of our friendship!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.210
Really?

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:28.780
Hooray!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:30.360
I really wanted this!

00:21:30.360 --> 00:21:31.890
Thank you, Tokunosuke!

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.420
Now we’re the best of friends!

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:39.570
He’s happy for getting a card?
He’s so self-absorbed.

00:21:39.570 --> 00:21:42.380
He was going to give back
a card that he wanted.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:48.280
Observation #9:
Even Yuma has a “behind.”

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.020
This is the last one.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.270
You must be kidding...

00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:03.090
Wait!

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:08.190
Why?!

00:22:12.430 --> 00:22:15.030
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:17.840
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:22.000
Rai Rider attacks Chew
Bone in defense position.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:24.490
Will you destroy it or not?

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:34.680
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:39.880
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:54.280
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:59.480
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:01.900
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.530
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:07.140
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.140 --> 00:23:08.820
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:13.440
Let’s say I wrote
the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:18.040
Will that change the future a year
or a decade from now?

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:23.380
The world I drew
at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:28.090
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:33.220
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:36.950
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:44.650
Esper Robin came to this city!

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:48.530
He must know something
about my memories!

00:23:48.530 --> 00:23:51.240
I told you that it’s haction!

00:23:51.240 --> 00:23:58.290
But Robin’s actor Fuya is struggling
between his real self and Robin’s fantasy.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:01.460
That’s when many incidents
occurred in the city!

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:09.840
Lavish Justice! Esper Robin Arrives!!

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:06.670
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Lavish Justice! Esper Robin Arrives!!”

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:09.970
Lavish Justice! Esper Robin Arrives!!

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:09.120
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.710 --> 00:24:15.190
Rai Rider destroys Chew Bone!

00:24:15.990 --> 00:24:20.920
You can destroy it when the ATK
is greater than the DEF!
